# Open cylinder: genus 0 with two boundary loops (an annulus).
#
# V - E + F = 468 - 1332 + 864 = 0. Note that chi = 0 here matches torus.obj, which
# is a *closed* genus-1 surface -- so this pair distinguishes code that computes
# topology from code that guesses it from the Euler characteristic alone.
#
# Two boundary loops also make it not a disk, so it is the mesh for checking how
# parameterization behaves when its disk assumption is violated but a boundary
# does exist.
#
# Developable: Gaussian curvature is 0 everywhere, so an isometric flattening
# exists and a correct conformal map should find it -- a sharper test than a
# curved patch, because the exact answer is zero area distortion.
# Radius 1, height 2, wound outward.

v 1 0 -1
